1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,480
Senile purpura affects up to 30 percent of adults over 75, those dark bruises that show up on your arms with no memory of bumping anything.

2
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:10,560
There are three main reasons behind it.

3
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:16,800
First, years of sun exposure break down collagen in the skin, especially on the hands and forearms.

4
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:20,720
That makes the skin thinner and leaves blood vessels with less support.

5
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:29,040
Second, blood thinners like aspirin make it easier for blood to leak out once a vessel tears, so the bruise spreads much larger than it should.

6
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:34,720
Third, dry skin loses its elasticity, so it absorbs even less impact than before.

7
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:40,960
Here is the reassuring part: these bruises usually fade on their own within one to three weeks and leave no scar.

8
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:42,880
Still, a few habits help.

9
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:47,200
Cover your hands and forearms with long sleeves or sunscreen before you head outside.

10
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:52,560
Keep track of the medications you are taking, and check with your doctor if bruising gets frequent or severe.

11
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:59,760
And moisturize daily, since a 12-week study found that daily retinol cream actually thickened skin and boosted collagen.

12
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:05,200
Bruising easily is not something to worry about, it just means your skin needs a little more care.
